    "1650392705a005a490": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "165039270565b4aa81-1": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "UPS",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>We utilize cardboard and paper packing materials for all of our shipping boxes. Our boxes are secured using an eco friendly paper tape.</p><p>When possible, we use  our own, in-house recycled cardboard as packing material.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "165039270565b4aa81-2": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "XPO/ Freight",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p><strong>Pallet wrap</strong>:<br/><br/>Pallet wrapping is required for items such as buckets, Eco Jugs, bag-in-box products, and mixed or miscellaneous boxes. These pallets must be wrapped using our <strong>readily biodegradable plastic wrap</strong>.<br/>Proper wrapping is a safety requirement. Without plastic wrap, items can shift or fall during transit, creating hazards for drivers and at distribution terminals. Wrapping the entire pallet keeps all items stable and secure throughout shipping.<br/>While ratchet straps work well for <strong>uniform items</strong> like barrels, they are not sufficient for pallets containing mixed products. In these cases, plastic wrap is necessary to ensure safe handling and delivery.<br/>Our plastic wrap is both <strong>biodegradable and recyclable</strong>. It can be recycled at any Walmart location with a plastic bag return station. If it were to enter the environment, it is designed to fully biodegrade in approximately two years, breaking down into humus.<br/>We are deeply committed to sustainability and eco-friendly practices. However, in certain shipping situations, plastic wrap is the safest and most responsible option to ensure products arrive intact and people remain safe.<br/></p><p><strong>Ratchet Straps</strong>:<br/>Our ratchet straps are reusable and can be purchased for ongoing use with our Close The Loop system. To ensure your straps are returned to you specifically, please mark them with your name using a marker or paint pen after you receive your order. This will help us avoid confusion with the straps from our other Close The Loop participants. Ratchet straps are used with barrels only!<br/></p><p><strong>Gaylord boxes</strong>: <em>Not currently available</em><br/>Gaylord boxes are available for purchase as an alternative to pallet wrapping. They are ideal for items unsuitable for ratchet straps, such as eco jugs, buckets, bag-in-box, and miscellaneous items. Please note:  barrels cannot be placed inside these boxes. For example, an order of three barrels and twelve eco jugs would require two separate pallets. If you purchase a Gaylord box, the eco jugs will be placed inside it.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
